From 77a2d01c1ecc8548620a1d0edbd4910e327f9e86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:17:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 361/638] [AROS] Define transferable Mojo channel endpoints

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: mojo-platform-endpoint-foundation
ROOT_CAUSE: PlatformChannel returned invalid endpoints on AROS because the POSIX fd model cannot represent task-owned Exec transport.
FIX_REASON: Add a MEMF_PUBLIC two-ended channel identity, cross-Process atomic ownership, Mojo ABI encoding, and command-line endpoint transfer without fd remapping.
SCOPE: mojo/public/c/system/platform_handle.h; mojo/public/cpp/platform/BUILD.gn; mojo/public/cpp/platform/aros_channel.{cc,h}; mojo/public/cpp/platform/platform_channel.cc; mojo/public/cpp/platform/platform_channel_endpoint.cc; mojo/public/cpp/platform/platform_handle.{cc,h}
VALIDATION: Exact AROS mojo_cpp_platform archive compiles and links at -j32; first missing CHECK_GT include failure was isolated and corrected.
RISK: This commit establishes endpoint identity and transfer only; MessagePort byte delivery is the next commit and NamedPlatformChannel remains unavailable.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: invalid socketpair stub -> shared address-space handle model -> MEMF_PUBLIC endpoint state -> Mojo platform ABI -> child command-line transfer.
